From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: a playlist player starts at its presentation

A BD-J application starts a playlist player (Player.start()) and libbluray
fires the JMF StartEvent and starts the media clock at once, when the
reader starts. The player shows the first picture later: it reads ahead,
and may change the display mode first (several seconds). Applications time
their own UI from StartEvent with wall-clock timers - M3GAN 2.0 opens its
menu bar 1.5 s after StartEvent and closes it 7 s later - so the viewer
sees what is left of it once the picture appears.

Opt-in with bd_bdj_set_defer_start() (requires presentation timing, patch
13). The playlist player's C start (bdpriv_select_rate(START)) takes the
start position and queues a start marker under bd->mutex, before the
reader runs. The application's StartEvent, MediaPresentedEvent and media
clock wait until the player releases the marker - presents the first
picture - with the start instant it passes (bd_bdj_release_ex). The
reader's statuses for the start are buffered behind StartEvent. An
application action on the player (stop, seek, rate, close) delivers the
start first. A player flush keeps a held start's own items
(BD_BDJ_RELEASE_FLUSH). A start not reported within 15 s starts anyway,
logged as an error.

Replaces patch 16 (shifting the media clock over a held start), which
moved only JMF media time and never the application's timers.

